  "title": "Farabbi2020: Motor-Imagery EEG dataset during robot-arm control",
  "description": "Motor-imagery EEG recorded from 12 healthy, BCI-naive participants performing cued left- versus right-hand imagery to control a Baxter robot arm reaching toward objects. Each participant completed three sessions with first-person and third-person visual feedback conditions, using 32 EEG channels at 250 Hz. This BIDS re-release was produced via MOABB from the original Zenodo deposit.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was acquired with a Brain Products LiveAmp 32 and actiCAP active Ag/AgCl electrodes (32 EEG channels plus 3 misc, 250 Hz). Each session had four motor-imagery runs of 40 trials (20 left, 20 right), with a 2 s baseline and 4 s imagery per trial. Online visual feedback was given, plus a resting-state recording.",
